{"availability":"available","full":"Kerneta/daidocs","name":"daidocs","description":"Open plain-text file format for AI memory. Your assistant's long-term memory as .dai files on your disk: readable by Claude, GPT, Gemini, Cursor, local models and grep (all LLM models work). MCP server + hooks for Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, Windsurf, Codex. 83% LongMemEval-S (GPT-4o), 92% (Claude Fable 5), 10x fewer tokens.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":53,"forks":5,"created":"2026-09-13T08:29:01Z","updated":"2026-10-07T12:33:54Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://daidocs.com","topics":["agent-memory","ai-agents","ai-memory","chatgpt","claude","claude-code","context-engineering","cursor","file-format","llm","local-first","long-term-memory","longmemeval","mcp","mcp-server","memory","open-standard","persistent-memory","plain-text"],"demo":"https://daidocs.com/demo.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T18:00:56.270Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T18:00:56.270Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T18:00:56.270Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:19.781Z","stars":46,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:34:57.294Z","stars":46,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-06T22:53:38.654Z","stars":45,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-08T12:58:59.955Z","stars":49,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-10T21:02:37.550Z","stars":52,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-16T18:00:56.270Z","stars":53,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Your assistant's memory becomes files on your disk that you can open, grep and keep: .dai for documents and session history, .cai for a graph of your code.","One of the most complete memory systems there is. Most tools remember one half: either your conversations or your code. This remembers both, in the same plain-text, local-first format, and a router knows which half a question belongs to.","Second on the LongMemEval-S leaderboard among memory systems anyone can re-run, 22.40 points above the same model with no memory, reading 10x fewer tokens per question. The .cai code graph answers callers, callees and rename-impact from a small fraction of the tokens of reading the files."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kerneta/daidocs/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"12920fbb0cdacb3543658f088f87997bacbf93c970c5cec728230dcfff80a02e","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T12:58:59.955Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T12:58:59.955Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Your assistant's memory becomes files on your disk that you can open, grep and keep: .dai for documents and session history, .cai for a graph of your code.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kerneta/daidocs/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The graph is deterministic, built by tree-sitter rather than a model, so it needs no API key and costs nothing to keep fresh.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kerneta/daidocs/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"The graph is deterministic, built by tree-sitter rather than a model, so it needs no API key and costs nothing to keep fresh.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kerneta/daidocs/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"12920fbb0cdacb3543658f088f87997bacbf93c970c5cec728230dcfff80a02e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kerneta/daidocs/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T12:58:59.955Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T12:33:54Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kerneta/daidocs/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T12:58:59.955Z","hash":"12920fbb0cdacb3543658f088f87997bacbf93c970c5cec728230dcfff80a02e","originalBytes":46151,"storedBytes":46151,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T12:58:59.955Z","qualityPriority":false,"enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:53.933Z","latestRelease":{"name":"V4.4n32: launch release","tag":"V4.4n32","publishedAt":"2026-09-18T16: